1. AIM

To develop a simple data link layer that performs flow control using Sliding Window and loss recovery using Go-Back-N.

2. THEORY
Sliding Window
Multiple frames can be sent before receiving acknowledgements.
The window moves forward when acknowledgements are received.
Example: Window size = 4 → frames 0,1,2,3 are sent first.
Go-Back-N
If a frame or its acknowledgement is lost, the sender goes back to that frame.
It retransmits the frames in the current window.
Example: If frame 2 is not acknowledged, frames 2,3,4,5 are retransmitted.
3. ALGORITHM
Read number of frames.
Read window size.
Send frames equal to the window size.
Read acknowledgement number.
If acknowledgement is valid, slide the window.
If acknowledgement is missing/invalid, go back and retransmit.
Continue until all frames are sent.
4. PROGRAM — SHORT VERSION
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int frames, win, ack = 0, i;

    printf("enter no.of frames\n");
    scanf("%d", &frames);

    printf("enter window size\n");
    scanf("%d", &win);

    while (ack < frames)
    {
        for (i = ack; i < ack + win && i < frames; i++)
            printf("Frame %d has been transmitted.\n", i);

        printf("\nPlease enter the Acknowledgement number: ");
        scanf("%d", &ack);

        if (ack > i)
        {
            if (ack == frames)
                printf("Total frames were sent");
            else
            {
                printf("invalid and resending the frame\n");
                ack = i - win;
            }
        }
    }

    return 0;
}

